{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThis epic tracks remediation of findings from the 2026-06-18 principal-engineer\nmaintenance audit of rebar (code debt, smells, architectural decay, separation\nof concerns, doc accuracy, unit/dir size). The audit ran deterministic scans\n(ruff/radon/vulture/ast-grep/jscpd/Serena) feeding seven single-perspective\nsubagents, then an **adversarial validation pass** (four subagents that read\nevery citation first-hand and tried to refute each finding). The re-run recipe\nand tool list live in `docs/maintenance-audit-runbook.md`.\n\n**Overall state: the codebase is healthy.** 0 mutable default args, 0 real bare\n`except:`, only 2 high-confidence dead-code items, 2 TODO markers, no `__all__`\ndrift, no orphan modules, no unreachable code, the tree is clean for its own ruff\ngate, and test investment tracks risk. The two load-bearing boundaries (the\nengine `sys.path` seam and the LLM optionality/lazy-import contract) are intact\nand runtime-verified. The debt is **localized and nameable**, captured in the\nchild stories below.\n\nSeverities below are the **validation-corrected** ones (several initial findings\nwere overstated and were downgraded after first-hand refutation; one was struck\nentirely — see `docs/maintenance-audit-runbook.md` for the methodology lesson).\n\n## Children (in recommended execution order)\n\n1. **[HIGH] Route `graph/_links.py` link writes through the canonical `_store` write path** — the one confirmed structural violation: a second write path bypassing the mandated single locked core.\n2. **[HIGH] Run the LLM-optionality degradation tests in a no-extras CI lane** — the optionality safety-net (10 always-skipped test instances) currently runs in zero CI lanes.\n3. **[MED] Documentation-truth sweep** — README still documents a deleted bash engine; event-schema version + event-type drift; one actively-false source comment; archive completed planning docs.\n4. **[MED-HIGH] Refresh the module-size offenders table + give the CI size report teeth** — table is 50% stale; CI check is a warn-only `echo`.\n5. **[MED] Fix the unresolved-alias blocker edge that can mis-report a ticket as ready** — the one validated wrong-answer broad-except; harden the answer-affecting sites.\n6. **[MED] DRY the validated duplication clusters (F9/F4/F5/F2-F3/F7)**.\n7. **[MED] Reduce accidental complexity in the reconciler differ/applier**.\n8. **[LOW] Dead-code removal + low-severity hygiene cleanups**.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All 8 child stories exist as children (`parent_id`) of this epic with detailed implementation plans and citations.\n- [ ] The two HIGH stories (graph write-path unification; optionality CI wiring) are completed first.\n- [ ] Each story's own acceptance criteria are met and verified before it is closed.\n- [ ] This epic is closed only after all children are closed or deferred-with-reason.\n</content>\n- [ ] Every child story is closed (or explicitly deferred with a recorded reason).\n- [ ] No regression in the existing ruff gate (`ruff check src tests` for `E,F,W,I,UP,B`), the scoped mypy gate, or the default test suite.\n- [ ] `docs/architecture.md`, `README.md`, `docs/event-schema.md`, and CLAUDE.md agree with the code on the facts the audit flagged.\n- [ ] The module-size CI report and the documented offenders table no longer disagree.\n- [ ] The LLM-optionality degradation path is exercised in at least one CI lane."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785007289303468001,"uuid":"29c0e69a-353a-48e0-a4fa-bbcb0ee950e2"}